From 54d1601aed524698a7ce180357eea2ab1c6f9cd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:16:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 890/913] drivers: stm32: ltdc: check the firewall restore
 result on error path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When applying the pin control state fails, stm32_ltdc_init restored the
non secure firewall configuration without checking the result, so the
LTDC could silently be left accessible from the secure world only.

Panic as already done when the same configuration is restored in
stm32_ltdc_final.

Coverity issue: CID 1207485: Unchecked return value in stm32_ltdc_init

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 79164d2b7e4ab7bdd8a8b2e89b5daf9ec513bf4f drivers: stm32: ltdc: check the firewall restore result on error path]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Iee556594569de6c26bf018d4e335d938ae1cbc1d
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/597011
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yannick FERTRE <yannick.fertre@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Philippe CORNU <philippe.cornu@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_ltdc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_ltdc.c b/core/drivers/stm32_ltdc.c
index 97a1b6e8a..0eb3f3da4 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_ltdc.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_ltdc.c
@@ -168,7 +168,8 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_ltdc_init(void *device)
 	if (ldev->pinctrl) {
 		ret = pinctrl_apply_state(ldev->pinctrl);
 		if (ret) {
-			firewall_set_alternate_conf(ldev->nsec_conf);
+			if (firewall_set_alternate_conf(ldev->nsec_conf))
+				panic("Firewall: Cannot set ltdc to no secure");
 			goto err;
 		}
 	}
